4rf, f' = 0.1rf − 0.4f. Drawn as rabbits across, foxes up, from three starts.\n\nWhich one should I make next? 👇\n\n#math #science #shorts","tags":"math, science, chaos, math art, math animation, physics, satisfying, shorts"},"about":{"title":"Foxes and Rabbits (Lotka–Volterra)","sources":[{"label":"Lotka–Volterra equations","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lotka%E2%80%93Volterra_equations"}],"math":"Rabbits r and foxes f: r' = 1.1r − 0.4rf, f' = 0.1rf − 0.4f. Drawn as rabbits across, foxes up, from three starts.","aha":"More rabbits → more foxes → fewer rabbits → fewer foxes → more rabbits. Each start gives its own closed loop: a quantity (0.1r − 0.4 ln r + 0.4f − 1.1 ln f) never changes, so nothing settles and nothing dies out.","why":"Lotka (1910) and Volterra (1926), the latter to explain fish catches in the Adriatic after the First World War; Hudson’s Bay Company lynx and hare records show the same cycles."}},{"name":"An Epidemic: Flattening the Curve (SIR)","mode":"2d","transport":{"duration":30,"bpm":90},"view":{"xMin":-1.45,"xMax":1.45,"yMin":-2.5778,"yMax":2.5778},"sequence":{"enabled":false,"past":"keep"},"layers":[{"name":"R₀ = 3","type":"ode","exprs":{"x":"-0.3*x*y","y":"0.3*x*y-0.1*y","z":"0.1*y"},"width":2,"colorMode":"gradient","color":"#ff5a5a","color2":"#ffd166","wave":"e-piano","volume":0.9,"samples":2000,"sim":{"x0":0.99,"y0":0.01,"z0":0,"dt":0.1,"skip":0,"cx":0.5,"cy":0.16,"scale":2.6},"caption":"S' = −βSI,  I' = βSI − γI,  R' = γI"},{"name":"R₀ = 1.5","type":"ode","exprs":{"x":"-0.15*x*y","y":"0.15*x*y-0.1*y","z":"0.1*y"},"width":2,"colorMode":"gradient","color":"#5ee0ff","color2":"#7bd389","wave":"triangle","volume":0.5,"samples":2000,"sim":{"x0":0.99,"y0":0.01,"z0":0,"dt":0.1,"skip":0,"cx":0.5,"cy":0.16,"scale":2.6},"octave":1,"caption":"-"},{"name":"Closing chord 1","type":"function","exprs":{"y":"-0.08","z":"0"},"hidden":true,"caption":"-","start":25.8,"end":0,"samples":40,"wave":"sine","volume":0.45,"width":1,"color":"#ffffff"},{"name":